          "name": "Usage Kicker",
          "fill": "#8B5CF6",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "PEN LIBRARY + FLUTTER",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "LU2",
          "name": "Usage Title",
          "fill": "#F8FAFC",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "How developers should consume this library",
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 28,
          "fontWeight": "800"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "LU3",
          "name": "Usage Body",
          "fill": "#A7B0C0",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "1. Reuse canonical component origins/refs in Pen for new screens.\n2. Map each design component to a Flutter presentation widget.\n3. Keep BLoC, repositories, services, API contracts and OrderLifecyclePolicy outside the component layer.\n4. Use semantic Variables rather than copying hex/spacing values.\n5. Device 360/390/430 is a QA/reference axis only; Flutter remains constraint-driven.\n6. Current product appearance is Light. Do not invent Dark mode.\n7. Arabic is RTL; all visible numerals use Western 0–9 with bidi-safe mixed text.",
          "lineHeight": 1.6,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "500"
        }
      ]
    }
